FFmpeg (LGPL build) bundled with EdgeSlicer on Linux
====================================================

The file `ffmpeg` in this folder is an unmodified, statically linked build of FFmpeg @DESC@ for @ARCH@,
made by the BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds project and redistributed here as a separate program. EdgeSlicer's phone hub
runs it as a child process (through go2rtc) to re-encode camera streams for the phone's Quality steps; it is
not linked into EdgeSlicer.

Licence: GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3 (the text is in FFMPEG-LICENSE.txt in this folder).
The build is configured with --enable-version3 and WITHOUT --enable-gpl or --enable-nonfree, and with
--disable-libx264 --disable-libx265, so it contains no GPL components. Its software H.264 encoder is
libopenh264 (Cisco OpenH264, BSD-2-Clause). It also contains other free libraries that BtbN's build
statically links (dav1d, libvpx, opus, freetype, zlib, OpenSSL and others); their licences are those of
the respective projects, listed with the build scripts below.

Where it came from
  Release:   https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds/releases/tag/@TAG@
  Archive:   @ASSET@
  SHA-256:   @SHA256@
  Mirror:    https://github.com/aceRage/edgeslicer-deps/releases/tag/ffmpeg-n8.1.3-btbn-2026-10-01 (the same archive,
             byte-identical, kept permanently; BtbN removes old releases)
  Build recipe (every library, version and patch used): the BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds repository at the commit the release
             tag points to; a copy of that commit is in the mirror release (btbn-ffmpeg-builds-recipe-*.tar.gz)

Corresponding source
  FFmpeg:    commit @COMMIT@ (release branch 8.1, `git describe`: @DESC@). A copy of the source at exactly that commit
             is in the mirror release (ffmpeg-source-*.tar.gz); upstream: https://git.ffmpeg.org/ffmpeg.git
  The other libraries: from their own projects, at the versions named in the BtbN recipe above.

Written offer
  If you received this EdgeSlicer package and want the source code of the FFmpeg build in it, or help replacing it
  with a build of your own (the hub uses whatever executable is at this path), the source is available from the
  mirror release named above, without charge, and will stay there for at least three years from the date of the
  release you received. For anything not in the mirror, ask through https://github.com/aceRage/EdgeSlicer/issues
  and it will be sent at no charge beyond the cost of the medium if one is needed. You may also replace the
  `ffmpeg` file with any other build: EdgeSlicer only needs an executable named ffmpeg with the libopenh264 encoder
  here, and falls back to a system ffmpeg or to no re-encoding when it is missing.

